Blog posts start with YAML front matter (title, date, tags). It is not useful prose for retrieval, so drop it:
def load_notes(folder):
for path in sorted(Path(folder).rglob("*.md")):
text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
if text.startswith("---"): # drop YAML front matter
end = text.find("\n---", 3)
text = text[end + 4:] if end != -1 else text
yield path.relative_to(folder).as_posix(), text
Always pass encoding="utf-8". On Windows the default is often a legacy code page (see Dev Essentials 01 · Text Encoding).

